  "street_name": "Elsworthy Road",
  "decision_date": "07/11/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development by itself and cumulatively with other recently granted extensions at upper floors and roof level, would overwhelm the host building resulting in an incongruous and dominant addition by reason of its bulk, massing and design, causing harm to the character and appearance of the Elsworthy Conservation Area and the setting of the Primrose Hill Grade II Listed Park and Garden. Additionally, the extensive glazing would result in excessive light spill, causing harm to the setting of the Primrose Hill Grade II Listed Park and Garden, contrary to policies D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of its significant height and depth of the ground floor extension along the western boundary, would result in harm to the amenity of the occupants of No.47 by way of creating an increased sense of enclosure and loss of outlook, contrary to policies A1 (Managing the impact of development) and D1 (Design) of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
